lds a slug | enumerate each `DAYS` codec's parameter space inside the slug gate | high: D20 established the pattern |\n197\t| 138 | other compressors under a text wrapper: zlib (`7801`/`785e`/`789c`/`78da`), raw deflate (no header), bz2, xz, lzma-alone (`5d0000`), under base64/base64url/hex/base32/base85/binary | seen D22 (zlib `78da` level 9 in std padded base64, 136 B single/TT; Mastery line 22 = 20-char per-fragment zlib streams `eNrL`/`eNpL`/`eNor`/`eNqr`); rest prebuilt tgt:compression-family-sweep; D21 solver `_b64z` sniff is `0x78`-only (fix: prebuilt tgt:zlib-header-sweep) | yes | b64 prefix `eJ`/`eNo`/`eF`/`eAE` zlib, `QlpoOTFBWSZT` bz2, `/Td6WFo` xz, `XQAAg` lzma-alone; hex `78..`, `425a68`, `fd377a585a`; raw deflate = no magic, high entropy | wrapper decode -> magic sniff -> `zlib.decompress(b, wbits)` (15 / -15 / 31 / 47 auto) / `bz2` / `lzma` (FORMAT_ALONE too) | done for zlib (D22); bz2/xz/raw deflate/other wrappers: med (a third compression day) |\n198\t| 139 | gzip/deflate stream quirks: headerless deflate, truncated/missing CRC trailer, FNAME/FCOMMENT/FEXTRA header fields, multi-member / concatenated gzip, non-zero mtime | prebuilt tgt:raw-deflate-gzip-quirks | yes | `H4sICA..` (FNAME flag 08: a filename in the header), several `H4sI` inside one string, gzip.decompress EOFError | `zlib.decompressobj(31)` (+ loop over `unused_data` for members); `wbits=-15` for raw; read FNAME/FCOMMENT as possible hints | high: knob on D21's codec |\n199\t| 140 | compressed bytes whose inflated text is ANOTHER seen codec (gzip of hex/rot13/Morse...), or an old transform over the compressed wrapper (reversed / rot13 base64 of gzip) | prebuilt tgt:decompress-then-redecode | yes | inflated output not English (hex / Morse / b64 again); b64 that only decodes after `[::-1]` / rot13 (`U4fV` = rot13 `H4sI`) | re-run the full pipeline (decode_chunk + CANDIDATES) on the inflated text, depth-capped; undo free transforms before the b64 sniff | high: stacking a seen family on the