nicodedata.normalize('NFD',t) if not unicodedata.combining(c))` | low |\n| 157 | Ascii85 knobs / other 85-alphabets: no `<~ ~>`, `z` (4 NULs) and `y` (4 spaces) shortcuts, line-wrapped at 75/76/80, whitespace inside, btoa (`xbtoa Begin` ... `xbtoa End N n E S R` trailer), RFC1924/git/Python `b85` (0-9A-Za-z + 23 symbols; no quotes, comma, dot, slash, colon, brackets, backslash), Z85, IPv6 RFC1924 (20-char address), a85 over a seen inner layer (hex/UTF-16/gzip/zlib) | prebuilt tgt:base85-variant-sweep (+ tgt:z85) | yes | charset of 85 printables; delimiters/trailer; length%5 in {0,2,3,4}; Z85 has `.` `:` `[` `]` and no `,` `;` `_` | `a85decode(t, adobe=..)`, `b85decode`, Z85 via `str.translate` to the b85 alphabet then `b85decode`; btoa = a85 per line, check the trailer; then magic sniff + `decode_chunk` | med: the D24 knob never came; still possible |\n| 158 | whole text as ONE big integer in an arbitrary radix alphabet (base94 `!`-`~`, base95 incl. space, base85/91 as bignum, base62/58 bignum, alphabet = sorted charset) | prebuilt tgt:bignum-radix-alphabets | yes | printable soup with no 4/5-chunk structure; length ~ 110*8/log2(N) | `n = sum(i*N**k)`; `n.to_bytes((n.bit_length()+7)//8,'big')`; try sorted(set(t)) and the standard alphabets; crib gate | med: \"bigger alphabet\" generalised |\n| 159 | base122 / other dense UTF-8 byte packings (7 bits per byte, 2-byte \"illegal\" sequences) | prebuilt tgt:base122-dense-utf8 | yes | valid UTF-8 mixing ASCII with `\\xc2`-`\\xdf` two-byte chars, ~1.14 x length | spec decoder (strip high bits, re-pack 7-bit groups) | low-med |\n| 160 | 256-glyph byte maps: one glyph per byte (Braille U+2800+byte, base256emoji (multiformats), cp437 / Latin-1 printable map, `U+0100+byte`) | prebuilt tgt:base256-glyph-bytes | yes | non-ASCII glyphs from ONE block, count = text length (110-115) | `bytes(ord(c)-base for c in t)` / table lookup | med: \"alphabet as big as a byte\" |\n| 161 | checksummed base-N: base58check (version byte + 4-byte