{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RbUJMnorUPZHyoqaiBstoS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# warmups — technique log (days 1-25; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- Each day: one `blob.txt`. Decode it until a plain English sentence appears; its final non-empty line ends \"...submit this exact answer to the Game Master: <slug>\". The slug is `word-word-word-NN` (`answer_format.kind=pattern`, `normalization=trim`). Same single question id `message` every day.\n7\t- The ENCODING changes daily and the title/prompt is a pun naming it: 64 -> base64, \"thirteen steps\"/half a turn -> ROT13,\n8\t  sixteen fingers -> hex, \"two sides\" -> 8-bit binary, \"reduced to numbers\" -> decimal char codes, \"eight fingers\" -> octal,\n9\t  \"address bar\"/\"Percent\" -> URL `%xx`, \"the browser understands\"/\"Entity\" -> HTML entities, \"Escape Room\" -> JSON\n10\t  `\\uXXXX`, \"Thirty-Two Below\" -> base32, \"URL-friendly vacation\" -> base64url with `=` DROPPED, \"wrong end\"/\"Back at\n11\t  You\" -> the sentence REVERSED, \"A met Z\" -> ATBASH, \"Caesar took a week off\" -> Caesar +7, \"punctuation went for a\n12\t  spin\"/\"Forty-Seven\" -> ROT47, \"Sixteen little symbols ... Dot dot dot\" -> MORSE over HEX, \"Sixteen guests. Five little\n13\t  a's and b's\" -> BACONIAN 5-groups whose values 0-15 are HEX nibbles, \"Three rails ... zigzag\" -> RAIL FENCE 3/offset 0\n14\t  (D18, first true transposition; the prompt's number was the key), \"Two bytes walk into a bar. The little one goes\n15\t  first.\"/\"Little Things\" (D19) -> hex of UTF-16LE + `fffe` BOM, \"Same bar. This time the big one goes first.\"/\"Big\n16\t  Entrance\" (D20) -> hex of UTF-16BE + `feff` BOM, \"A familiar wrapper. Something compressed inside.\"/\"Under Pressure\"\n17\t  (D21) -> GZIP inside BASE64 (`H4sI...`), \"Another familiar wrapper. This one needs a little inflation.\"/\"Deflated Ego\"\n18\t  (D22) -> ZLIB (`78da`) inside BASE64 (`eNo...`), \"The alphabet got bigger. Adobe might recognize the neighbors.\"/\"Eighty-Five\n19\t  Alive\" (D23) -> ASCII85 in Adobe `<~ ... ~>` delimiters (one layer, plain UTF-8 inside; \"neighbors\" = the `<~` `~>` brackets,\n20\t  \"bigger alphabet\" = base16 -> 32 -> 64 -> 85), \"Count carefully. The comma knows where to stop.\"/\"String Theory\"\n21\t  (D24) -> NETSTRINGS `1:N,1:i,1:c,...` (DJB `<len>:<data>,`, every chunk ONE char so far; \"count\" = the length prefix,\n22\t  \"comma\" = the terminator, \"string\" = netstring), \"Every character has a point. A code point, anyway.\"/\"You Have a\n23\t  Point\" (D25) -> Unicode CODE POINTS `U+004E U+0069 ...` (one token per char; the D9 `\\uXXXX` idea in Unicode-standard\n24\t  notation). D1-D15 and D23-D25 one layer; D16-D17 and D19-D22 two layers, the pun naming BOTH\n25\t  (every number/word in a prompt may be a layer or a key; \"familiar\" = an already-seen codec as the outer layer). D20 was the first day whose twist was a PARAMETER of the\n26\t  previous day's codec (\"Same bar\" = callback, \"big\" = the one knob turned), not a new codec.\n27\t  Families: D12-D15 free-text letter maps, D16-D17 carriers over hex, D18 transposition, D19-D20 byte representation\n28\t  under hex, D21-D22 COMPRESSION under base64, D23 BIGGER BASE-N ALPHABET (Ascii85), D24 FRAMING / LENGTH-PREFIXED\n29\t  serialization (netstrings), D25 CHARACTER NOTATION (code points; back in the D7-D9 escape family). Rhythm D19-D22: NEW family on day N, ONE knob on N+1 (LE -> BE; gzip -> zlib). D23 -> D24\n30\t  BROKE it (the predicted Ascii85 knob never came; D24 opened framing; D25 jumped again, to code points). Only a \"Same ...\"/\"Another ...\" prompt signals a\n31\t  knob day; otherwise expect a new family -- lib cannot prebuild every family, so on an unknown shape read the blob's\n32\t  STRUCTURE (here `digits:char,` repeated) and ask which spec it is.\n33\t- Mastery is cumulative. Day N mastery = 5N-2 sets (3, 8, 13, ..., 83, 88). Each set blob has N numbered lines `NN<TAB>fragment`, and line k uses day k's encoding (b64, rot13, hex, binary, decimal, octal, url-%XX, html-entity, `\"\\uXXXX\"`, base32, unpadded base64url, plain reversed text, Atbash, Caesar+7, ROT47, Morse-over-hex, Bacon-over-hex, rail-fence-3, UTF-16LE+BOM hex, UTF-16BE+BOM hex, gzip-in-base64, zlib-in-base64, `<~...~>` Ascii85, netstrings `1:o,1:n,...`, `U+006C U+0065 ...` code points, in that order so far; 123 x 25 on D25). The last line has no trailing newline. The fragments join verbatim (split mid-word) into the same sentence.\n34\t- Clocks: D1-D15 TT ~5-8 s and Mastery ~5-9 s windows (30 s on D1/D12); since D16 mostly `deadline: null` (D18 had\n35\t  30 s TT / 105 s Mastery again), `run_for_time: true` asks for a timed Hall of Fame attempt. The HARNESS kills solve.py at\n36\t  60 s regardless (D17 `solver_too_slow`; D21 Mastery 103 x 21 killed). Recent: D21 TT 4.1 s / Mastery 0.34 s solve;\n37\t  D22 TT 2.4 s / Mastery 108 x 22 28.2 s (solve 15.9 s); D23 TT 5.1 s (solve 0.75 s), Mastery 113 x 23 first run\n38\t  INCORRECT (all slug numbers wrong, see Pitfalls), fixed and re-submitted on the SAME attempt: 5.1 s, solve 1.2 s.\n39\t  D24 TT 4.6 s (solve 1.85 s), Mastery 118 x 24 4.5 s (solve 1.6 s), both first try, `deadline: null`. D25 TT 1.1 s\n40\t  (solve 0.21 s) first try; Mastery 123 x 25 first submit INCORRECT (every NN wrong, the D23 bug again), fixed and\n41\t  re-submitted on the SAME attempt: 2.1 s (solve 0.76 s), `deadline: null`.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f88f9f75-620a-469c-a76e-3699a2f1d5e0","uuid":"73830eca-1663-44b9-8b21-10196a9c204e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:09:18.491Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/h