'\\n')+'\\n'+rows.rstrip('\\n')+'\\n'+t[i:]\n# recognition cues\nrep(\" U+XXXX / %uXXXX / \\\\U0000XXXX -> chr(int(h,16));  =XX / soft \\\"=\\\\n\\\" -> quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME\\n\",\n\" U+004E U+0069 (D25, 7 B/char) / %uXXXX / \\\\U0000XXXX / \\\\u{4E} -> chr(int(h,16)); mixed prefixes -> one alternation tokenizer\\n   LATIN SMALL LETTER I / \\\\N{..} -> unicodedata.lookup;  =XX / soft \\\"=\\\\n\\\" -> quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME\\n\")\nrep(\" invisible U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF -> zero-width stego;  ASCII-looking with odd bytes -> homoglyphs (Cyrillic)\\n\",\n\" invisible U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF -> zero-width;  U+E00xx tags -> cp-0xE0000;  FE00-FE0F/E0100.. selectors -> bytes;\\n   one non-ASCII block, ord-ord(crib) constant -> code-point offset;  runes/Greek/Cyrillic, lengths kept -> crib map\\n\")\nrep(\" lines 19/20 own BOM (LE+BE in one blob), 21/22 own gzip/zlib streams, 23 own `<~..~>`, 24 own `1:c,` netstrings. NEVER pre-decode a line in place\\n before decode_chunked (D23: plain `el-46` got ROT5 -> all 113 NN wrong) -- register_free(name, day, fn) instead.\\n\",\n\" lines 19/20 own BOM (LE+BE in one blob), 21/22 own gzip/zlib, 23 own `<~..~>`, 24 own `1:c,`, 25 own `U+XXXX` tokens.\\n NEVER pre-decode a line in place (D23 ROT5'd `el-46`; D25 `_unknown_line_cands` mangled plain `le-52`: all NN wrong)\\n -- register_free(name, TODAY'S DAY, fn) on the RAW line, even when the whole-blob step already decodes single/TT.\\n\")\n# readiness gaps json\na=t.index(\"```json\\n\", t.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"))+8; b=t.index(\"\\n```\", a)\nG=json.loads(t[a:b])\nbyid={g['id']:g for g in G}\nfor gid in [\"netstring-knobs\",\"indexed-fragments-shuffled\",\"tnetstrings\",\"bencode-sexp\",\"length-prefix-binary-tlv\"]:\n    byid[gid]['priority']=2\n    byid[gid]['detail']=\"BUILT (prebuild ok). \"+byid[gid]['detail']\nfor gid in [\"string-builder-literals\",\"resp-redis\",\"http-chunked-transfer\",\"asn1-der-tlv\",\"delimited-field-framing\"]:\n    byid[gid]['priority']=3\n    byid[gid]['detail']=\"BUILT (prebuild ok). \"+byid[gid]['detail']\nbyid['rhythm-broken-structure-first']['detail'] += \" D25 confirmed the pattern (third new family in a row: code points, a D9 sibling); the prebuilt row-22 decoder caught it, so keep the queue wide across families.\"\nbyid['mastery-line-routing']['detail'] += \" D25 REPEATED the bug through another path (123/123 sets NN wrong): _uplus_lines pre-decoded line 25 and, with no day-25 codec registered, decode._positional sent the plain line to _unknown_line_cands, which re-decoded it. Checklist for every new day: (1) register_free(name, day, fn) for TODAY's day number; (2) the whole-blob step must skip numbered Mastery blobs; (3) print one set's joined sentence and compare NN with the raw last line before submitting.\"\nbyid['byte-family-mastery-cost']['detail'] += \" D25 (123 x 25): solve 0.76 s.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"unicode-character-names\",\"concept\":\"Unicode character NAMES per character (`LATIN CAPITAL LETTER N, LATIN SMALL LETTER I, SPACE, ...`, `\\\\N{...}`)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Most likely D25 sequel ('every character has a point' -> 'has a name'). Decoder names_dec(t): split on , ; newline | or detect `\\\\N{..}`; each token -> unicodedata.lookup (case-insensitive, also aliases like 'HYPHEN-MINUS', 'FULL STOP', 'DIGIT FIVE'); whole text must resolve or None. Also accept `U+004E LATIN CAPITAL LETTER N` (UnicodeData.txt line style) and lowercase names. Register in CANDIDATES + decode_chunk + as a free codec for Mastery fragments (5-10 names per line). Fixtures: comma list, newline list, \\\\N{} string, UnicodeData lines, decoys (English prose in caps).\"},\n {\"id\":\"codepoint-notation-knobs\",\"concept\":\"code-point notation knobs: `\\\\u{4E}`, `\\\\x{4E}`, short `U+4E`, lowercase `u+`, no separators, decimal/octal code points with prefixes, `\\\\N{U+004E}`\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 knob on D25 (U+